        "description_cTHNm8": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description": "<p>Pongal is one of the oldest harvest festivals of Tamil Nadu, celebrated for over 2,000 years as a thanksgiving to nature, farmers, cattle, and the Sun God (<em>Surya</em>). Observed during the Tamil month of Thai, Pongal marks prosperity, renewal, and new beginnings. The word <em>Pongal</em> means “to boil over,” symbolizing abundance and overflowing happiness.</p><p>Wearing new clothes on Thai Pongal is a deeply rooted tradition, and for generations, Kanchipuram silk sarees have been considered the most auspicious traditional Pongal dress. Their pure silk texture, rich zari work, and temple-inspired motifs make them the best dress for Pongal, reflecting both cultural pride and festive elegance.</p><p>At Cavirk, the Pongal Dress for Women 2026 collection is exclusively curated with authentic Kanchipuram sarees. This page is designed for women searching for a Pongal dress, Pongal dress for ladies, traditional Pongal saree, or the best dress for Pongal, all in one trusted destination.</p>",
            "font_size": 14,
            "font_weight": "body_weight",
            "spacing_bottom": 10
          }
        }
      },
