        },
        "description_tpgMqP": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description": "<p>Pongal celebrations span four days—Bhogi, Thai Pongal, Mattu Pongal, and Kaanum Pongal—each honoring nature, livestock, and family bonds. Historically, silk sarees were worn during Pongal as a symbol of wealth, purity, and gratitude. Even today, a traditional Pongal saree is an essential part of festive rituals, temple visits, and family gatherings.</p><p>This cultural importance is why Kanchipuram sarees continue to dominate Pongal dress collections and remain the most preferred Pongal costume for women across generations.</p>",
            "font_size": 14,
            "font_weight": "body_weight",
            "spacing_bottom": 10
